Hoi Jacqueline,

I would just do a single loop over sites and then define two separate random effects, here is a sketch:

for(i in 1:nsites){

    NK[i] ~ dpois(lambdaK[i])

    etaK[i,s] ~ dnorm(0, tauK)
    log(lambdaK[i,s]) <- beta0K + beta1K * dist_ms[i,s] + beta2K * water_temp[i,s] + beta3K * elev[i,s] + beta4K * pool[i,s] +
    beta5K * riffle[i,s] + beta6K * depth_avg[i,s] + beta7K * lwd[i,s] + beta8K * timber_area[i,s] + beta9K * rip_area[i,s]  +

    etaSite[i] + etaStream[Stream[i]]
       etaSite[i] ~ dnorm(0, tau.eta.site)
}
for(i in 1:nstream){
  etaStream[i] ~ dnorm(0, tau.eta.stream)
}

Here, Stream is an vector of length 'nsites' which contains the stream membership of each site.

Best regards  --- Marc

