> I've built the full model (all site covariates included) and am now looking to reduce the model. Our goal is to determine if the abundance of the non-native/dominant species is affecting the abundance of the native/subordinate species. And whether those interactions are affected by habitat covariates.
>
> From what I've read there appears to be many ways to go about it.
> - Sequentially removing covariates if the 95% credible interval of the posterior distribution included 0. (i.e. https://esajournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/ecs2.1229). Is this a common process?
> - DIC or WAIC. Although DIC appears to be contentious?
> - Bayes factor
>
> Do you have any suggestions on the best way to select a model/reduce the number of covariates in this case?
>
> Best,
>
> Jacquie
